From 282896e7d18181599e9f7bf81725d6d1ec023549 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:03:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover vm_page_telemetry.c

Reconstruct the page telemetry ring and its CoreAnalytics drain path
from the reference kernel: the static ring entry, dedupe table and lock
state, the Jenkins-hashed dedupe probes and compare-and-swap marking,
the per-process zero-wired-pages event, the one-shot drain thread call
and the two emit entry points with their single-argument overload.

The panic message keeps the reference's line number through a #line
directive so the drain-thread allocation failure reports the same
location.

Remaining explicit stubs: 62.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
---
 osfmk/vm/vm_page_telemetry.c | 485 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 osfmk/vm/vm_page_telemetry.h |  87 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 522 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)

